---
metaTitle: Why Provident | What sets our grading apart
metaDescription: Full attention for ancient coins, tokens and medals, holders and labels designed for the coin, and certificate records open to anyone.
eyebrow: Why Provident
heading: What a collector should expect of us.
intro: A grading company is trusted for what it does, not what it says. These are the commitments we hold ourselves to.
sections:
  - mark: laurel
    title: Ancient coins, given full attention
    text: Roman Republican and Imperial coins and select Greek types are central to our work. At the services that include it, they receive expanded identification, a recorded weight, and separate subgrades for strike and surface, so the label describes the coin as a specialist would.
  - mark: medal
    title: Tokens and medals, on equal terms
    text: Most tokens and medals are accepted, and they pass through the same examination, attribution and grading as coinage, rather than being treated as an afterthought.
  - mark: pen
    title: Holders that complete the coin
    text: Our labels began as a conviction that a holder should be worthy of the coin inside it. Each design is themed to its subject, from classical to modern, and custom designs can be created for a collection, a dealer or an auction.
  - mark: holder
    title: Sealed to the industry's methods
    text: Every holder is sonically welded around the coin, forming a permanent, tamper-evident seal. We use the same sealing techniques and machinery as other third-party grading services.
  - mark: registry
    title: Records open to inspection
    text: Every certificate we issue is recorded, and anyone can check it on this website. A grade that can be verified is worth more to the next owner than one that must be taken on trust.
  - mark: coin
    title: Room to begin small
    text: Collectors, coin shops and auction houses all send coins to us. If you would like to see our work before sending a larger group, a small trial submission is welcome.
coda:
  title: See the work for yourself.
  text: A small trial submission is welcome.
  links:
    - label: Submissions
      href: /submit
